# Documentation and handoff

- Update `docs/current-state.md` and `docs/session-handoff.md` after substantial work.
- Update `docs/project-state-report.md` at milestone completion (and major interruptions).
- Maintain append-only `docs/milestones.md` when milestones complete.
- Distinguish: session-handoff (immediate resume) vs project-state-report (milestone state) vs milestones (history).
- Append entries to `docs/chat-workflow-log.md` (do not overwrite history).
- Update module docs and `docs/platform-roadmap.md` when status changes.
- Create ADRs from `docs/adr/ADR-000-template.md` when required by governance.
- Cite code paths when documenting implemented architecture.
- Mark unverified facts as “To be verified”—never invent migration heads, test counts, or feature completeness.
